1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,703
In early 2024, 3M reported its 2023
revenue as 32.7 billion dollars.

2
00:00:05,703 --> 00:00:09,358
A year later, the same year read 24.6
billion.

3
00:00:09,358 --> 00:00:11,583
Eight billion dollars, gone.

4
00:00:11,583 --> 00:00:17,780
An analyst needs to know why, and the
answer is scattered across many filings.

5
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:19,850
This is Tiresias.

6
00:00:19,850 --> 00:00:24,409
It asks why, step by step, and backs each
step with evidence.

7
00:00:24,409 --> 00:00:25,679
This run is live:

8
00:00:25,679 --> 00:00:32,180
every read goes through Zetaris, and
NVIDIA Nemotron gives the critic a second
opinion.

9
00:00:32,980 --> 00:00:33,898
Three voices.

10
00:00:33,898 --> 00:00:37,500
Tiresias proposes a cause and measures it
with SQL.

11
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:39,830
The Sphinx, our critic, tests it:

12
00:00:39,830 --> 00:00:43,220
is it a real cause, and do the numbers add
back?

13
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:47,153
Here it hits a wall.

14
00:00:47,153 --> 00:00:51,025
The drop points to a spin-off, but 3M's
own data can't measure it.

15
00:00:51,025 --> 00:00:53,020
So it asks before it goes looking.

16
00:00:53,820 --> 00:01:00,484
Tiresias searches the filings and finds
the new company the spin-off created, even
though the names have nothing in common.

17
00:01:00,484 --> 00:01:04,060
I approve, and Zetaris registers its data
while the run continues.

18
00:01:08,020 --> 00:01:11,162
The Sphinx adds that company's revenue
back.

19
00:01:11,162 --> 00:01:17,302
The gap left is 126 million, just 1.6
percent of the change, so the cause is
accepted.

20
00:01:17,302 --> 00:01:18,087
The answer:

21
00:01:18,087 --> 00:01:20,800
re-base 2023 on continuing operations.

22
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:23,299
The chips show what served the run:

23
00:01:23,299 --> 00:01:27,940
Zetaris, Nemotron through Meterless
Nightshift, and H-MEM memory.

24
00:01:28,753 --> 00:01:34,505
That second opinion is a real model call,
and the trace names the model that
answered.

25
00:01:34,505 --> 00:01:37,314
Models suggest; SQL and the critic decide.

26
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:41,984
Click any link to see the SQL and the rows
behind it.

27
00:01:41,984 --> 00:01:43,880
No claim without evidence.

28
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:49,483
What worked becomes a lesson in Meterless
H-MEM:

29
00:01:49,483 --> 00:01:50,933
a path, not an answer.

30
00:01:50,933 --> 00:01:56,600
A similar question about GE recalls it,
and the run takes three steps instead of
five.

31
